        "original_id": "e3b79be6-42f3-55a7-9c9e-4efbc942c950",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Timanfaya National Park, Sierra Nevada National Park, Lanzarote, Canary Islands, Granada, Almería, Málaga, Andalusia, Alpujarra, El Marquesado, Lecrin Valley, Spain\n- Topics: Spanish national parks\n\nFacts:\n- Timanfaya National Park is a Spanish national park in the southwestern part of the island of Lanzarote in the Canary Islands.\n- Sierra Nevada National Park is a national park in Andalusia, Spain, located in the provinces of Granada, Almería, and Málaga.\n- Sierra Nevada National Park stretches from the Alpujarra to El Marquesado and the Lecrin Valley.\n- Sierra Nevada National Park covers a total area of 85,883 hectares.\n- Sierra Nevada National Park is the largest national park in Spain.",
